  "tagline": "Disk-friendly Postgres vector extension using IVF + RaBitQ, the successor to pgvecto.rs.",
  "description": "VectorChord (vchord) is a PostgreSQL extension from TensorChord that replaces its earlier pgvecto.rs. It builds on pgvector's data types but uses IVF partitioning with RaBitQ quantization instead of in-memory HNSW, which makes index builds much faster and lets large indexes live mostly on disk with good recall. The companion VectorChord-bm25 extension adds BM25 ranking for hybrid search. It suits teams who started on pgvector and hit build-time or memory walls in the 50M to 1B vector range but want to stay in Postgres.",
